# Provider failover chain: GEMINI is the PRIMARY, OpenRouter is SECOND, DeepSeek direct is the
# THIRD/FALLBACK. All three are optional and additive: set one key for a single provider, more
# to fail over between them, none for the honest-null (no-model) path. On a runtime failure that
# happens BEFORE the first byte reaches the reader (rate limit / 5xx / network / auth), the app
# advances to the next configured provider and retries; once anything has streamed it does not.

# Gemini (primary). OpenAI-compatible endpoint, so no extra SDK is needed. NOTE: Gemini 3 models
# CANNOT fully disable thinking, and gemini-3.7-flash also REJECTS the 'minimal' level (400), so
# the app asks for the lowest level it accepts ('low') with thoughts hidden — as close to off as
# the model allows (thinking tokens are still billed). If you switch GEMINI_MODEL, its accepted
# thinking levels may differ. Reasoning mode is shared across providers via DEEPSEEK_REASONING_EFFORT.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.7-flash
GEMINI_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai/

# OpenRouter (second). Reached only if Gemini is unset or fails before the first byte.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# Optional overrides. The default model is minimax/minimax-m3:free — the free deepseek-v4-flash
# slug was RETIRED by OpenRouter (it 404s and points to the paid deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash).
# Free tiers rate-limit often (that is what the DeepSeek fallback is for); to run the paid
# DeepSeek model through OpenRouter instead, set OPENROUTER_MODEL=deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash.
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=minimax/minimax-m3:free
# OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# Optional OpenRouter free-tier attribution headers:
# OPENROUTER_APP_TITLE=Mindstack
# OPENROUTER_APP_URL=

DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-v4-flash
DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com
PORT=8787

# Reasoning policy — SHARED across ALL providers, translated per provider. Two separate layers:
#   (1) OUR custom reasoning: a scripted planning pass the model writes in the content stream,
#       split off and shown as the live "thinking" murmur. Steerable (edit the prompt) and truly
#       capped (its tokens are output-only). Provider-agnostic.
#   (2) the model's NATIVE reasoning: DeepSeek `thinking`, OpenRouter `reasoning`, Gemini
#       `thinking_level` — billed against max_tokens, hard to steer, effort is a bias not a cap.
# RECOMMENDED = prompted: custom reasoning ON, native reasoning OFF (DeepSeek/OpenRouter) or
# MINIMAL + hidden (Gemini 3.x cannot fully disable it, so it runs at its 'low' floor).
#   prompted -> custom planning pass ON, native reasoning off/minimal   (DEFAULT; recommended)
#   none     -> everything OFF: no planning pass AND no native reasoning (fastest, no murmur)
#   low/high/max -> native reasoning ON at that level, and NO custom planning pass
#   default  -> native reasoning at the model's own server default, and NO custom planning pass
# NOTE: tsx watch does NOT reload .env — fully restart the server after changing this.
DEEPSEEK_REASONING_EFFORT=prompted
